    "body": "CMake builds `ctime_tests` when Valgrind headers are available, but CTest does not run it. Register it under Valgrind with `--error-exitcode=42`, or run it directly when MemorySanitizer is enabled.\n\nFor Valgrind builds, omit registration with a configure-time message if the executable is unavailable or the build is cross-compiled. Add a test label and document the existing opt-out.\n\nAddresses the CMake part of #1560. Autotools integration remains separate.\n\nTested on x86_64 Linux with GCC 15.2.0, Clang 21.1.8 and Valgrind 3.26.0:\n\n- All 226 CTest tests pass with the default module configuration.\n- The MSan build runs the test directly and passes, even with Valgrind installed.\n- A deliberately introduced branch on poisoned secret data makes CTest fail through Valgrind; restoring the source makes it pass.\n- Checked registration with constant-time tests disabled, Valgrind support disabled, an empty Valgrind executable setting, and a cross-compilation configuration (`CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=Linux` with the host compiler).\n",
